THE ACCEPTANCE PASS:
  CLCPA-270  PROTECTION COMES FROM THE LABEL, AND THE FIGURE FROM WHOEVER
     CAN SUPPLY IT. Open A3 2023 in Report Data. Its Total row must have NO
     editable label and NO delete control, and its 2,354,317 must still be
     TYPEABLE -- that is the A8 ruling: the engine cannot derive that figure,
     so it stays the preparers. Same shape on A8 2025 "Total CES Programs
     Installations" (336,599). Then open B1: its Total row must be locked in
     FULL, values included, because the engine does derive it. Every total
     row on every table must still READ as a total row, shaded, whether or
     not its cells are typeable.
  CLCPA-274  THE TEMPLATE SAYS WHICH TOTAL COLUMNS IT COMPUTES.
     Download H1s template. Its Grand Total column must read (calculated) on
     the body rows, not sit blank inviting a figure. Then TYPE A NUMBER over
     one and import: it must be ACCEPTED and reconciled, never discarded --
     the marker is guidance, not a rejection. Open F6s template, which has a
     second header row: that header row must NOT carry the marker.
  CLCPA-278  A TOTAL THAT AGREES WITH ITS PARTS FOLLOWS AN EDIT.
     In H1, edit a component cell of a row whose Grand Total currently EQUALS
     its parts: the total must move with it. Then edit a component of a row
     whose total already DISAGREES: that total must be KEPT untouched and the
     advisory raised instead. Nothing stored may move until you save.
  CLCPA-269  THE SAVE COUNT IS WHAT THE PREPARER BROUGHT.
     Import a file into an EMPTY year and open the Save dialog. The count
     must be the cells you actually filed -- not the label column, not the
     rows the engine computes. On the shape this was filed against it read
     20 and must now read 12.
  CLCPA-276  A NOTICE LIVES EXACTLY AS LONG AS THE DRAFT IT DESCRIBES.
     Raise any import notice, then press Reset: it must go. Raise one and
     SAVE: it must go. Raise one, switch table or year and come back: it must
     not be describing a draft that no longer exists.
  CLCPA-277  A FILE NAMED FOR THE WRONG YEAR IS NAMED.
     Rename a template to carry a different year and import it into another.
     A RED box must say so, on the staged dialog AND after loading, and the
     import must still go through -- it is advisory only. A filename with no
     year, or two, must say nothing.
  CLCPA-275  THE NOTICE STACK CLEARS THE CARD BELOW IT.
     With one or more notices showing at the bottom of the panel, the gap
     below the last one must match the spacing stacked cards already use
     elsewhere. This one is your eye: no harness here can see a rendered gap.

